- Restore root: `/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/m4-23-commercial-s0-restore/20260828T16-50-53Z`

The encrypted remote stream hash matched the local archive and the commercial
archive inventory gate passed. Safe extraction, application/Control Git checks,
venv import and config/state comparisons passed. The restore rehearsal then
stopped before creating its temporary database because local `postgres` could
not traverse the root-private restore evidence path to open
`commercial-s0-database.dump`.

No temporary database exists and no live path was changed. The correction keeps
the restore root private: the root operator opens the already inventory-checked
custom dump and passes it through standard input to `pg_restore --list` and the
isolated temporary-database restore. The temporary database remains protected
by an exit trap and is dropped after verification. No ACL, group or permission
is widened.
